{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id1201255374"}, "name":{"label":"GPT not approved"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2026-10-09T10:36:52-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.2026.272"}, "id":{"label":"14646697859"}, "title":{"label":"Disappointing"}, "content":{"label":"frustrating and increasingly not worth using\n\nI’m genuinely considering deleting this app after how frustrating my experience has become.\n\nI use ChatGPT for creative projects that genuinely matter to me, including making pictures and posters for my Facebook gifting group. I enjoy being able to send pictures, show products, keep track of prices and work with ChatGPT to create things I’m excited about.\n\nBut lately, I’m constantly running into restrictions that stop me from doing what I came here to do. I can’t always send pictures, I run into limits on how much I can use it, and it feels like every time I want to get something done, there’s another barrier in the way.\n\nToday has been the final straw. I was preparing a Christmas Most Wanted poster, collecting items and prices so I could get it posted in time for an event starting at 8 pm, when people could help by finding and gifting the items. I had been working towards this all day, only to find that picture uploads were unavailable until much later than I’d expected.\n\nI wasn’t expecting to have to plan my day around upload restrictions, and I wasn’t made aware of how much these limits could interfere with what I wanted to do. I understand that services may need usage limits, but when those limits disrupt something time-sensitive, it is incredibly frustrating.\n\nWhat makes this worse is that I rely on the app for creative support and enjoy having longer conversations while working on projects. Having restrictions affect pictures, image creation and conversation length makes the experience feel increasingly limited.\n\nI was already having a difficult day, and something that should have been enjoyable ended up causing me more stress. I shouldn’t have to fight with an app just to make a poster.\n\nI know no app can offer unlimited usage, but the limits need to be clearer, more predictable and better communicated. Users should have a reasonable understanding of what they can do before investing time in a project.\n\nRight now, I’m questioning whether it’s worth continuing to use ChatGPT at all. It’s disappointing because I genuinely enjoy what I can create with it when it works as expected.\n\nPlease improve the transparency around usage limits and give users a more reliable experience. People use this app for real projects, with real deadlines, and these restrictions can have a genuine impact.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=6448311069&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}], "updated":{"label":"2026-10-20T11:26:44-07:00"}, "rights":{"label":"Copyright 2008 Apple Inc."}, "title":{"label":"iTunes Store: Customer Reviews"}, "icon":{"label":"http://itunes.apple.com/favicon.ico"}, "link":[
